; A runtime-sized global with no GPU binding is a CPU/audio-only value
; (e.g. a load-wav'ed sample buffer). WGSL has no representation for an
; unsized array outside a storage binding, so shader output must simply
; omit it — emitting it produces a module the GPU rejects at runtime.

(var samples: [f32])

@fragment
(defn f []: vec4f
  (vec4f 1. 0. 0. 1.))
